{"id":"quadratic-equations","title":"Maths: quadratic equations","subject":"Mathematics","label":"JAMB · WAEC","exams":["jamb","waec"],"language":"en","seconds":181,"duration":180.51,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":506,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Garden puzzle","start":0,"end":14.285},{"id":"explain","title":"The form","start":14.285,"end":44.085},{"id":"explain2","title":"Formula and roots","start":44.085,"end":73.525},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":73.525,"end":104.495},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":104.495,"end":115.535},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":115.535,"end":132.995},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":132.995,"end":149.505},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap and tip","start":149.505,"end":180.51}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":7.94,"text":"Ada has a rectangular garden. Its length is two metres longer than its width, and the area is twenty-four square metres.","w":[0.5,0.75,0.99,1.11,1.85,2.34,2.59,3.02,3.21,3.45,3.88,4.31,4.62,4.87,5.3,5.54,5.79,6.1,6.28,7.02,7.45]},{"s":0,"a":8.24,"b":13.86,"text":"What is the width? I'm Kora, and today we solve questions like this with quadratic equations.","w":[8.3,8.48,8.62,8.74,9.8,10.02,10.78,10.9,11.26,11.44,11.74,12.16,12.34,12.54,12.72,13.26]},{"s":1,"a":14.71,"b":20.87,"text":"A quadratic equation has the form a x squared plus b x plus c equals zero, where a is not zero.","w":[14.78,14.86,15.42,15.94,16.14,16.26,16.62,16.9,17.06,17.6,17.92,18.3,18.52,18.82,19.16,19.42,19.8,20.08,20.24,20.36,20.54]},{"s":1,"a":21.17,"b":26.16,"text":"It can have at most two roots. A root is a value of x that makes the equation true.","w":[21.24,21.34,21.52,21.74,21.88,22.16,22.38,23.28,23.38,23.74,23.88,23.96,24.36,24.62,24.78,24.96,25.18,25.32,25.8]},{"s":1,"a":26.46,"b":33.15,"text":"One method is factorisation. When a equals one, find two numbers that multiply to give c and add to give b.","w":[26.6,26.78,27.12,27.28,28.5,28.8,29.04,29.5,29.8,30.12,30.34,30.66,30.84,31.42,31.52,31.76,32.12,32.36,32.54,32.64,32.88]},{"s":1,"a":33.45,"b":37.37,"text":"Write the two brackets, then set each bracket to zero and solve.","w":[33.5,33.76,33.88,34.08,35.04,35.3,35.62,35.82,36.22,36.36,36.82,37.02]},{"s":1,"a":37.67,"b":43.66,"text":"Factorisation is quick when it works. This simple version is for a equals one, with a little trial.","w":[37.7,38.52,38.74,39.02,39.18,39.26,40.2,40.46,40.78,41.26,41.42,41.84,42.06,42.48,42.72,42.9,42.96,43.2]},{"s":2,"a":44.51,"b":48.65,"text":"The quadratic formula always works, even when factorisation fails.","w":[44.54,44.68,45.22,45.8,46.14,46.98,47.2,47.4,48.16]},{"s":2,"a":48.95,"b":55.56,"text":"x equals minus b plus or minus the square root of b squared minus four a c, all divided by two a.","w":[49.08,49.34,49.7,50.1,50.46,50.96,51.12,51.5,51.62,51.9,52.12,52.22,52.42,52.82,53.14,53.38,53.54,54.32,54.5,54.9,55.08,55.36]},{"s":2,"a":55.86,"b":65.06,"text":"The discriminant is b squared minus four a c. Positive gives two different real roots. Zero gives equal roots. Negative gives no real roots.","w":[55.88,56,56.64,56.8,57.04,57.48,57.86,58.1,58.24,59.1,59.6,59.9,60.12,60.48,60.76,61.6,61.98,62.32,62.62,63.52,63.92,64.22,64.44,64.68]},{"s":2,"a":65.36,"b":73.1,"text":"For JAMB, remember sum of roots equals minus b over a, and product of roots equals c over a. JAMB loves this.","w":[65.4,65.58,66.34,66.76,66.98,67.1,67.48,67.8,68.18,68.38,68.72,69.28,69.44,69.8,69.92,70.32,70.68,70.98,71.28,71.98,72.4,72.7]},{"s":3,"a":73.95,"b":78.11,"text":"Solve x squared minus five x plus six equals zero.","w":[74.04,74.58,74.72,75.5,75.9,76.38,76.68,76.98,77.4,77.72]},{"s":3,"a":78.41,"b":84.52,"text":"We need two numbers that multiply to six and add to minus five. They are minus two and minus three.","w":[78.46,78.64,78.92,79.2,79.52,79.7,80.22,80.34,81.02,81.24,81.44,81.6,81.94,82.68,82.82,82.98,83.4,83.78,83.92,84.26]},{"s":3,"a":84.82,"b":88.38,"text":"So we write x minus two times x minus three equals zero.","w":[84.92,85.06,85.18,85.62,85.8,86.18,86.4,86.86,87.02,87.34,87.7,88.02]},{"s":3,"a":88.68,"b":92.26,"text":"Set each bracket to zero. x equals two or x equals three.","w":[88.78,89.04,89.24,89.6,89.78,90.28,90.5,90.8,91.24,91.5,91.68,91.98]},{"s":3,"a":92.56,"b":96.34,"text":"Both answers work, because each one makes the original equation true.","w":[92.6,92.96,93.3,93.88,94.28,94.58,94.74,94.96,95.12,95.58,96.04]},{"s":3,"a":96.64,"b":104.07,"text":"Check. Sum of roots is five, which equals minus b over a. Product is six, which equals c over a.","w":[96.7,97.5,97.74,97.88,98.24,98.42,99.06,99.34,99.68,100.14,100.5,100.82,101.32,101.74,101.88,102.44,102.72,103.1,103.5,103.84]},{"s":4,"a":104.92,"b":109.57,"text":"Now try this one. Solve x squared plus seven x plus ten equals zero.","w":[105,105.24,105.48,105.74,106.34,106.84,106.98,107.42,107.76,108.16,108.3,108.58,108.94,109.22]},{"s":4,"a":109.87,"b":112.91,"text":"Look for your two numbers first, then write the brackets.","w":[109.9,110.14,110.28,110.46,110.68,111.06,111.86,112.12,112.34,112.46]},{"s":4,"a":113.21,"b":115.11,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[113.26,113.56,113.86,114.02,114.3,114.6,114.78]},{"s":5,"a":115.96,"b":119.93,"text":"The roots are x equals minus two or x equals minus five.","w":[115.96,116.12,116.62,116.94,117.22,117.6,118.02,118.46,118.74,118.92,119.26,119.6]},{"s":5,"a":120.23,"b":126.51,"text":"The numbers two and five multiply to ten and add to seven, so the brackets are x plus two and x plus five.","w":[120.23,120.36,120.74,120.96,121.12,121.48,121.98,122.12,122.46,122.62,122.78,122.9,123.74,123.88,124,124.48,124.76,124.92,125.22,125.56,125.78,125.9,126.14]},{"s":5,"a":126.81,"b":132.57,"text":"Check the sum: minus two plus minus five is minus seven, which equals minus b over a.","w":[126.84,127.08,127.22,127.98,128.36,128.6,128.92,129.28,129.68,129.8,130.14,130.9,131.2,131.54,131.96,132.3,132.52]},{"s":6,"a":133.42,"b":138.35,"text":"Watch for sign errors. The roots have the opposite signs to the numbers inside the brackets.","w":[133.48,133.74,133.9,134.2,134.94,135.08,135.38,135.54,135.74,136.16,136.56,136.7,136.84,137.32,137.72,137.82]},{"s":6,"a":138.65,"b":142.2,"text":"Never divide by x to cancel it, because you can lose a root.","w":[138.8,139.08,139.5,139.84,140.02,140.14,140.54,141,141.26,141.38,141.54,141.78,141.86]},{"s":6,"a":142.5,"b":149.08,"text":"In the formula, don't forget plus or minus. And always make one side zero before you factorise or use the formula.","w":[142.54,142.66,142.78,143.58,143.82,144.14,144.44,144.54,145.3,145.54,145.88,146.18,146.34,146.62,146.98,147.3,147.46,148.16,148.34,148.5,148.6]},{"s":7,"a":149.93,"b":156.76,"text":"Recap. A quadratic has the form a x squared plus b x plus c equals zero, where a is not zero.","w":[150,150.96,151.04,151.58,151.78,151.9,152.18,152.52,152.66,153.06,153.38,153.62,153.78,154.08,154.36,154.66,155.5,155.8,156,156.14,156.4]},{"s":7,"a":157.06,"b":162.69,"text":"Factorisation uses two numbers that multiply to c and add to b when a equals one.","w":[157.1,157.96,158.28,158.52,158.92,159.12,159.68,159.88,160.54,160.86,161.06,161.2,161.48,161.84,162.1,162.54]},{"s":7,"a":162.99,"b":167.78,"text":"The quadratic formula always works, and the discriminant tells the nature of the roots.","w":[163,163.16,163.78,164.38,164.74,165.5,165.62,165.72,166.36,166.64,166.78,167.12,167.22,167.32]},{"s":7,"a":168.08,"b":175.27,"text":"Exam tip: for JAMB, remember sum of roots equals minus b over a and product equals c over a.","w":[168.16,168.6,169.34,169.54,170.2,170.62,170.82,170.94,171.4,171.76,172.2,172.56,172.94,173.4,173.6,174.1,174.48,174.8,175.1]},{"s":7,"a":175.57,"b":179.91,"text":"Ada's garden is four metres wide, by the way. Keep practising with Knowzone.","w":[175.66,175.98,176.48,176.7,176.96,177.32,177.64,177.8,177.9,178.52,178.76,179.3,179.46]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Garden puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Rectangle: area = 24 m²"},{"at":0.4,"kind":"formula","text":"length = width + 2"},{"at":8.14,"kind":"text","text":"Find the width"},{"at":8.14,"kind":"text","text":"Solve using quadratic equations"}]},{"at":14.46,"heading":"Quadratic form","items":[{"at":14.61,"kind":"formula","text":"ax² + bx + c = 0, a ≠ 0"},{"at":21.07,"kind":"term","text":"Root","detail":"value of x making equation true; at most two roots"},{"at":26.36,"kind":"term","text":"Factorisation","detail":"a = 1: find two numbers × to c, + to b"},{"at":33.35,"kind":"text","text":"Write brackets; set each bracket = 0"},{"at":37.57,"kind":"text","text":"Quick when a = 1; needs trial"}]},{"at":44.26,"heading":"Formula and roots","items":[{"at":44.41,"kind":"text","text":"Quadratic formula always works"},{"at":48.85,"kind":"formula","text":"x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / 2a"},{"at":55.76,"kind":"term","text":"Discriminant","detail":"b² − 4ac; >0: two real; =0: equal; <0: no real roots"},{"at":65.26,"kind":"formula","text":"sum roots = −b/a"},{"at":65.26,"kind":"formula","text":"product roots = c/a"}]},{"at":73.7,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":73.85,"kind":"formula","text":"x² − 5x + 6 = 0"},{"at":78.31,"kind":"step","text":"−2 × −3 = 6; −2 + −3 = −5"},{"at":84.72,"kind":"formula","text":"(x − 2)(x − 3) = 0"},{"at":88.58,"kind":"formula","text":"x = 2 or x = 3"},{"at":96.54,"kind":"formula","text":"sum = 5 = −b/a; product = 6 = c/a"}]},{"at":104.5,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":104.5,"kind":"question","text":"Solve x² + 7x + 10 = 0."}]},{"at":115.71,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":115.86,"kind":"formula","text":"x = −2 or x = −5"},{"at":120.13,"kind":"step","text":"2 × 5 = 10; 2 + 5 = 7"},{"at":120.13,"kind":"formula","text":"(x + 2)(x + 5) = 0"},{"at":126.71,"kind":"formula","text":"−2 + −5 = −7 = −b/a"}]},{"at":133.17,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":133.32,"kind":"wrong","text":"Roots have same signs as bracket numbers"},{"at":133.32,"kind":"right","text":"Roots have opposite signs to bracket numbers"},{"at":138.55,"kind":"wrong","text":"Divide by x to cancel it"},{"at":138.55,"kind":"right","text":"Never divide by x; you can lose a root"},{"at":142.4,"kind":"wrong","text":"Forget ±; factorise before one side = 0"}]},{"at":149.68,"heading":"Recap and tip","items":[{"at":149.83,"kind":"formula","text":"ax² + bx + c = 0, a ≠ 0"},{"at":156.96,"kind":"text","text":"Factorisation: two numbers × to c, + to b (a = 1)"},{"at":162.89,"kind":"text","text":"Formula always works; discriminant gives root nature"},{"at":167.98,"kind":"tip","text":"JAMB: sum roots = −b/a; product roots = c/a"},{"at":175.47,"kind":"text","text":"Practise with Knowzone"}]}],"check":{"at":115.36,"seconds":10,"question":"Solve x² + 7x + 10 = 0.","answer":"x = −2 or x = −5"},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}